Hash Solution [Brute Force]
Approach:
Create temp to traverse 
Create unordered set that is Hashing 
[Hashing stores node and key that is frequesncy]
Traverse the linked list
If set that is nodeSet has temp value again then return true 
If no return false 
Insert temp in nodeSet and move temp to next 
Why to insert - to check if is it in linked list or not 

Time Complexity: O(N) 
HashSet - O(1) ---[O(1) * O(N)]

Space Complexity: O(N)
As HashSet stores that visited to that node 

Code:

class Solution {
public:
    bool hasCycle(ListNode *head) {
        ListNode* temp=head;
        std::unordered_set<ListNode*> nodeSet;
        while(temp!=NULL){
            if(nodeSet.find(temp) != nodeSet.end()){
                return true;
            }
            nodeSet.insert(temp);
            temp=temp->next;
        }
        return false;

    }
};



